{"id":"NCT07100080","title":"Study of Izalontamab Brengitecan (BMS-986507) Versus Platinum-based Chemotherapy With or Without Amivantamab for EGFR-mutated Non-small Cell Lung Cancer After Failure of EGFR TKI Therapy (IZABRIGHT-Lung01)","official":"IZABRIGHT-Lung01: A Randomized, Open-label, Phase 2/3 Study of Izalontamab Brengitecan (BMS-986507) Versus Platinum-based Chemotherapy With or Without Amivantamab in Patients With EGFR-mutated Non-small Cell Lung Cancer and Disease Progression on EGFR Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitor Therapy","summary":"A study of Izalontamab Brengitecan (BMS-986507) versus platinum-based chemotherapy with or without Amivantamab for EGFR-mutated non-small cell lung cancer after failure of EGFR TKI therapy","conditions":["Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Iza-bren"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Carboplatin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Cisplatin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Pemetrexed"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Amivantamab"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Non-squamous NSCLC, not amenable to treatment in curative intent.\n* Documented evidence of EGFR mutation (exon 19 deletion, L858R mutation).\n* Progressive disease on a 3rd-generation (such as osimertinib, furmonertinib, lazertinib,...) EGFR-TKI-based mono- or combination therapy regimen as the most recent line of therapy in an adjuvant, locally advanced, or metastatic treatment setting.\n* Eligible to receive a platinum-based doublet chemotherapy regimen (either cisplatin or carboplatin) in combination with pemetrexed with or without amivantamab.\n\nExclusion criteria:\n\n* Inadequate organ function and/or bone marrow reserve.\n* Leptomeningeal metastases or spinal cord compression.\n* Poorly controlled systemic medical conditions.\n* Other protocol-defined inclusion/exclusion criteria apply.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":661,"start":"2025-11-05","pcd":"2028-12-15","upd":"2026-11-12","sponsor":"Bristol-Myers Squibb","areas":["oncology","rare"],"central":["BMS Clinical Trials Contact Center www.BMSClinicalTrials.com · 855-907-3286 · Clinical.Trials@bms.com","First line of the email MUST contain NCT # and Site #."],"sites":[{"f":"UCI Health - Chao Family Comprehensive Cancer Center and Ambulatory Care building","city":"Irvine","pr":"California","zip":"92612","s":"R","lat":33.6695,"lon":-117.8231,"c":"Cathleen Park, Site 0279"},{"f":"University of California, Irvine (UCI) Health - UC Irvine Medical Center","city":"Orange","pr":"California","zip":"92868-3201","s":"R","lat":33.7878,"lon":-117.8531,"c":"Cathleen Park, Site 0154"},{"f":"Shaw Cancer Center","city":"Edwards","pr":"Colorado","zip":"81632","s":"R","lat":39.645,"lon":-106.5942,"c":"Erin Schwab, Site 0139 · 970-569-7608"},{"f":"Local Institution - 0085","city":"Gainesville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32610","s":"STOP","lat":29.6516,"lon":-82.3248,"c":""},{"f":"Local Institution - 0142","city":"Pembroke Pines","pr":"Florida","zip":"33028","s":"NYR","lat":26.0032,"lon":-80.2239,"c":"Site 0142"},{"f":"Piedmont Healthcare","city":"Atlanta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30318","s":"R","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"c":"Andrew Pippas, Site 0270 · 706-660-6449"},{"f":"John B Amos Cancer Center","city":"Columbus","pr":"Georgia","zip":"31904","s":"R","lat":32.461,"lon":-84.9877,"c":"Andrew Pippas, Site 0143 · 706-660-6449"},{"f":"Rush University Medical Center","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60607","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Helen Ross, Site 0153 · 312-942-5904"},{"f":"Dana-Farber Cancer Institute","city":"Boston","pr":"Massachusetts","zip":"02215","s":"R","lat":42.3584,"lon":-71.0598,"c":"Julia Rotow, Site 0067 · 617-632-6049"},{"f":"Washington University School of Medicine","city":"St Louis","pr":"Missouri","zip":"63108","s":"R","lat":38.6273,"lon":-90.1979,"c":"Ece Cali Daylan, Site 0091 · 314-273-8008"},{"f":"Renown Regional Medical Center","city":"Reno","pr":"Nevada","zip":"89502","s